    ## 4. Backend telemetry APIs and retention
    
    The central API exposes category history under `/api/v1/nodes/{node_id}/metrics/{category}` for `system`, `storage`, `network`, `services`, `processes`, `connections`, `containers`, and `vms`. `/api/v1/nodes/{node_id}/capabilities` reports what the host collector can access. Structured log events are available from `/api/v1/nodes/{node_id}/logs` with `since`, `until`, `severity`, `source`, `limit`, and `offset` filters. Alert active state is derived from the latest transition by node, alert name, and chart. Investigation creation returns HTTP 503 without writing a record until a worker is available.
    
    Metric snapshots default to 24 hours of retention (`METRICS_RETENTION_HOURS`). Structured logs default to 7 days (`LOG_RETENTION_DAYS`). Set these variables in the central `.env` file to adjust retention.
    
