## Assistant

There’s already a host installer, but it puts secrets in command-line arguments. I’m adding a central bootstrap that generates private credentials plus a minimal agent-only secrets file, and a host bootstrap that reads that file (or prompts without echoing secrets), writes `/opt/palantir-agent/.env.agent`, and enrolls the host. Neither script will print the secret values.

